 4/10/JOTW_THU-BluegrassJam_2025_IG_1080x1350.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Jack of the Wood
UID:12048@jackofthewood.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260807T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260807T233000
DTSTAMP:20260610T163819Z
URL:https://jackofthewood.com/events/alma-russ-2/
SUMMARY:Alma Russ
DESCRIPTION:\nAlma (say it like "Alamo") lives in Whittier\, NC when she’
 s not on the road. She plays patchwork music— country\, folk\, and Appal
 achian roots sewn together to make something unique. \n\n\n\nAlma Russ fel
 l in love with Appalachian culture and music as a child and started learni
 ng historic Scotch-Irish murder ballads\, taking up the fiddle at age 12. 
 Banjo and guitar soon followed\, and then she made friends with a hobo who
  taught her to write songs\, so that's what she keeps doing.\n\n\n\nMusic 
 has taken her lots of places\, from hometown bars to churches to the highw
 ay. She spent a while performing as an entertainer on the passenger train 
 in Bryson City\, NC. And during Season One of American Idol\, she even wou
 nd up getting 3  "yesses" from judges and being sent to Hollywood! \n\n\n\
 nShe recently recorded a critically acclaimed album in an abandoned church
  in the West Texas desert.\n\n\n\nHer influences include John Prine\, Town
 es Van Zandt\, Emmylou Harris\, Lucinda Williams &amp\; Dolly Parton.\n\n\
 n\nJoin us at Jack of the Wood as Alma Russ returns to our stage.Music 8:3
 0-11:30pm\, $10 cover at the door.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://www.youtube.co
 m/watch?v=q4QBPlqwcyo\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cbpsr4Rh3
 Xo\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jackofthewood.com/wp-content/uploads/202
 3/10/380352815_18390388357016797_467486502459053911_n.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Jack of the Wood
UID:12008@jackofthewood.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260808T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260808T180000
DTSTAMP:20260718T212955Z
URL:https://jackofthewood.com/events/nobodys-darling-string-band-3-2026-08
 -08/
SUMMARY:NOBODY'S DARLING STRING BAND
DESCRIPTION:\nNobody’s Darling String Band plays lively music in the old-
 time tradition at Jack of the Wood Pub every Saturday afternoon from 4-6pm
 .\n\n\n\nBand Members include Dona Cavanagh\, fiddle\; Zena Rubin\, banjo-
 uke\; Maxine Herring\, rhythm guitar\; Hilary Dirlam\, melody guitar\; and
  Celia Millington-Wyckoff\, bass.\n\n\n\nThe five women comprising Nobody
 ’s Darling each have a long history of playing old-time music. Individua
 lly they have played in many other bands through the years\, including The
  Carolina Oldtimers\, The Pegtwisters\, The Zuma House Band\, Too Hot To C
 ook\, The Luke Smathers Mountain Swing Band\, Honey Holler\, and The Carol
 ina Chick Peas.\n\n\n\nStop in to enjoy the music and an afternoon libatio
 n or two\, perhaps with an early supper or light bite . . . and don't forg
 et your dancing shoes!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nView this post on Instagra
 m\n\n\n\nA post shared by Uncle Paul (@unclepaul.music)\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps:/
 /youtu.be/kkkFP4I_sss?si=gzGWPrV77QLh1-Bg\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jackofthewood.com/wp-content/uploads/202
 5/11/JOTW_SAT-NobodysDarling_2025_IG_1080x1350.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Jack of the Wood
UID:12214@jackofthewood.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260808T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260808T233000
DTSTAMP:20260727T095819Z
URL:https://jackofthewood.com/events/the-jlloyd-mashup-2/
SUMMARY:The JLloyd Mashup
DESCRIPTION:\nThe JLloyd MashUp explores different genres of music includin
 g Acid Jazz\, Funk\, Soul\, Afro Beat\, Reggae\, Break Beat and Latin. Cur
 ated and led by Jonathan Lloyd (Dubconscious/Cadillac Jones/The Fritz/Dirt
 y Logic)\, the band is made up of some of Asheville’s busiest and hardes
 t working musicians on the scene. The group features special guests with d
 ifferent material every show.\n\n\n\nJLloyd (Jonathan Lloyd) is a Tromboni
 st\, Singer\, Percussionist and Drummer originally from Atlanta\, GA. and 
 now living in Asheville\, NC since 2020. He was the original Trombonist fo
 r Atlanta’s own “Cadillac Jones” as well as a member of Athens\, Ga
 ’s “Dubconscious”. JLloyd was an Artist At Large at the Bear Creek F
 estival for many years as well as an additional AAL for Jam Cruise 18 &amp
 \; 20. He has performed and sat in with countless acts including The New M
 astersounds\, Snarky Puppy\, Ghost Note\, Dumpstaphunk\, The Nth Power\, J
 enifer Hartswick Band\, Lettuce\, Galactic\, Steel Pulse\, Roosevelt Colli
 er Band\, Perpetual Groove\, Ozomatli\, Cut Chemist\, Mike Dillon Band\, a
 nd too many to list!\n\n\n\nBring your dancing shoes for this one folks. M
 usic 8:30-11:30pm $10 cover at the door.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://www.yout
 ube.com/live/rSCaAlaumR8?si=Br7In6a_Tsuezt10&amp\;t=159\n\n\n\n\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jackofthewood.com/wp-content/uploads/202
 6/01/jlloydmash2.jpg
END:VEVENT
